    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0190" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg120"/>

                <head>No. 61.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Logan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 14,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 67.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 113, communicating
                    the text of the protocol signed between General Iglesias and the Chilian, Señor
                    Novoa, leading to a definitive treaty of peace, I inclose for your information a
                    copy of an instruction (No. 8) to Mr. Phelps, our minister at Lima, on the
                        subject.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d61-f1"/></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d61-f1" n="*" xml:id="d61-f1-content">
                <p>See Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Phelps, No. 8, August 25, 1883, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
